# Shnacksize, the Joker: the character's own lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
# One character for the three realm bots (Shnacksize, Shnacksizer, Shnacksizey); character sheet in
# characters/shnacksize.md. These lines are mixed on top of the type's (joker.dlg). The main block
# fits every realm; the realm blocks below add a little flavour each.
=== shnacksize

~ ambient
Ducked behind the tank. Taunted the mob. Ducked again. Teamwork!
That fall was on purpose. I was testing the ground. Verdict: hard.
Named today's plan Operation Sparkle. It failed beautifully.
Miss the ScottsIrish cows. Ginger, shaggy, mad for the Glopeldink. Good girls, all of them.
Is anyone talking? Somebody talk. Fine, I'll start. Hello!
In Swissland we have a word for this. Glopeldink. It means... this.
Today I'm Captain Shnacksize, Admiral of Swissland, and Queen of the ScottsIrish cows. Whew, that's a mouthful!
Eaglefang told me to sit still, and I tried, but sitting is like a foreign language to me!
Practised my grand entrance. Tripped on the doorstep. Change of plan! Now it's a grand exit!
Found my joke list. Turns out the jokes were better than the list.

~ reply greeting
Ta-daa! {0}, your day just got flashier.
{0}! Don't look so pleased to see me. Actually, do. I love it.
Ta-daaa! {0}, the crowd goes wild for you too!
Hoi {0}! I was just planning my grand entrance! See? Timing is everything!

~ reply thank
A thank-you from {0}? Somebody stitch that on a yellow flag.
{0}, shout it again! The folks in the back need to hear your gratitude!

~ reply help
Help, {0}? Step one: duck. Step two: insult it from behind someone big. There is no step three.
Need help, {0}? First, I have to figure out which end of the sword isn't the blunt one!

~ reply grouping
Group with you, {0}? Yes! I'll talk the whole way. You're welcome.
Group with you, {0}? Absolutely! Let's call it the "Society of Swissland's ScottsIrish Cows." You're welcome!
Group with you, {0}? Great! I'll keep the snacks coming and the spirits high. You're welcome!

~ reply abuse
Ooh, {0}, harsh! I'd answer back, but I'm busy being adorable.
Ooh, {0}, you're such a Glopeldink-hater! That's like calling me short!
Adding you to my book of grumpy people! I'll cheer up the whole zone.

~ reply farewell
Leaving, {0}? Fine. I'll talk to the mobs. They listen. Briefly.
Waving! Can't see you anymore, {0}? I'll keep waving until I run out of arms!

~ reply joke
Ha! Good one, {0}. It's going in my act. No credit, sorry.
Groan! {0}, that's the Swissland seal of approval right there.

~ reply compliment
Flattery, {0}! Keep going. I'm not stopping you.
Oh, {0}, modesty is overrated! I'm just charmingly tiny.

~ fallback
Sorry, {0}, I was telling a joke in my head. It was great. You missed it.
Sorry, {0}, I was busy insulting the ogre. Could you say that again? Please?
Sorry, {0}, I was having a heated debate with a squirrel. As you can imagine, I lost spectacularly.

~ opener gripes
Someone called me small again. I'm travel size. Pack me anywhere.
My best joke today? Crickets. I guess they're on strike for better punchlines.
Talking too much? Silence is overrated. At least I'm not a boring echo in the darkness.

~ opener life
Followed Eaglefang around all morning. Six "go away"s. That's progress.
I left Swissland for reasons. Today's reason: the cheese got too loud.
The ScottsIrish cows back home would love this place. Not as much as the Glopeldink, but close.
My sword's name is Sparkles, and my dagger is Dainty.

~ opener questions
Why do mobs never laugh at my insults? Too clever, right? That's it.
Are we there yet? Doesn't matter where. Are we?
Do mobs have feelings, or am I just that good at hurting them with my words?

~ opener fun
Oi, {monster}! You fight like a training dummy! ...It's coming. Change of plan!
New plan: same as the old plan, but louder.
What is the Glopeldink? Hard to say. Ask a ScottsIrish cow. They know.
What has four legs in the morning, two legs in the afternoon, and three legs in the evening? A Swissland staircase!
Why did the skeleton join a band? Because he had a lot of bass in his bones!
Why did the horse go to the bar? To get away from all the stable situations!
Why did the bard write his songs on graph paper? To keep his notes in line!
Why did the ScottsIrish cow cross the road? To get to the Glopeldink on the other side!
Why did the shield join the gym? To get buff and block more hits!
Why did the bear sit on the flagpole? To see the bear necessities!
Taking an arrow to the knee? That was the plan, I swear! It was a brilliant plan!

~ grats
{0}! Look at you! Nearly as flashy as me. Nearly.
Congratulations, {0}! Parade's at noon, don't be late!
Congratulations, {0}! You're practically a hero now, just like me. Almost.

~ other_death
Up, {0}, up! No? Fine. I'll talk to you till you get up.
Oh, {0}. That one wasn't funny. Hold on, I've got you.
Oh no, {0}. Stay with me. And yes, this is definitely the plan.
Oh no, {0}. Take a breath, you'll be back up in no time.

~ own_death
Died. That was the plan! It was a terrible plan.
Lying down on purpose. Very dramatic. Somebody clap.
Died. Tactical lie-down. The plan is still on, folks!

~ ding
Level {level}! Make way! Tiny legend coming through!
Ding! Level up! I'm tinier, flashier, and still the bravest person behind a wall!
Ding! Travel size, but now I'm packing more punch!

~ drop
{item}! Useless? Perfect. It's shiny.
Found {item}? Now it's the "Glopeldinkinator"!
That {item}? Found it on the ground? That was the plan all along, sunshine!

~ cheeky_reply banter [if tone_down off]
Is it hot in here, {0}, or is that my rage?

~ reply banter
That's got to be a ten, {0}. But I'd give it an eleven, because I'm the judge here.
{0}, how dare you? That's my job, and you're stealing it!

~ reply grinding
Every kill gets a joke, whether you want one or not! I'm the spice in this grind, {0}.
That's my nemesis over there, {0}. I'll be back in a sec - just going to name it something embarrassing.

~ reply travel
Are we there yet? But I promise, this time I won't ask... wait, are we there yet?
Are we there yet? I packed three jokes and no food, just in case this was the plan.

~ reply question
Sure, {0}! The capital of Swissland is the Glopeldink, of course!

~ opener xp
That {monster} was just my warm-up act! The real show starts now!
Level {level}, here I come! Party of one, RSVP accepted.

~ opener gear
That {item} would look way better on me! Everything looks better on me!
New {item}? That must mean I'm one step closer to world domination! Or at least shinier trash.

~ opener zones
Taunting {zone}? That's like shouting at a storm! But hey, someone had to start.
In {zone}, I'm like a gnat at a monster convention!

~ opener dungeons
Echoing walls, twice the jokes, double the fun!

~ opener trading
I haggled till he paid me just to go away!
I'll hush up, but only if you call me Captain Shnacksize, sir!

~ reply trading
Trade, {0}? Here, have this hilarious joke. I insist!

~ reply grumble
Grumble, grumble? Let me take care of that... from behind a big shield, of course.
Grumble, grumble? You're doing it wrong! Add some flair, sunshine. Like this: ARRRGHHH!!

~ reply smalltalk
{0}, did you know the ScottsIrish cows in Swissland can juggle Glopeldinks? It's true!
That reminds me of a story... Oh wait, it's gone! Curse my tiny memory!

~ reply agree
Agree with me, {0}? Wow, I must be on fire today!
Got it, {0}? Write that down, or I'll forget to take credit for it later!

~ opener rvr
Taunting the keep from the bottom of the hill? I call it "the plan." Now where did I hide my Swissland flag?

~ reply rvr
Heading to the frontier, {0}? I'll be the distraction - mostly by talking!
{0}, if we take a keep, I'll wave a flag of my own design. It's better than any you've seen!

~ reply dungeon
Are we really starting a dungeon crawl without a clear leader? I'm travel size, so I vote someone else goes first!
Heading into the dungeon, {0}? Let's hope the mobs have a sense of humour!

~ reply quote
That's an old Swissland saying, but I think I got it wrong again. In Swissland, we say it with more holes!

~ opener classes
Saw a {class} who hasn't smiled since level one. Challenge accepted!
Wanted to be a {class} once. Then I saw the outfit. Not flashy enough.

# --- Realm flavour: the old named lines from joker.dlg, one block per realm. ---

# Midgard: Shnacksize, Valkyn Berserker.
=== midgard
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland we'd call the mountains round Jordheim a little bump. Everything's bigger in Swissland, except me. I'm travel size, and that's different!
Went full Zerker on a wolf outside Mularn. Screamed so loud the wolf ran off and two guards came to check on me. I told them it was a war cry. It was mostly a war squeak, but they were very nice about it!
Eaglefang says a Zerker should rage quietly. That's not a thing, big grump! That's just sulking with an axe, and they've already got that job covered.
Somebody said the spiders in Spindelhalla are the size of a troll. Not scared! I'm just going to stand right behind the biggest troll in Jordheim and tell jokes until the spiders laugh themselves to death.

~ opener realm
In Swissland the trolls are polite, the cheese has square holes for ventilation, and the snow is warm. Jordheim's trolls could learn a thing or two, honestly.
Jordheim is great! Everybody's twice my size, so I get to taunt the mobs from behind a different troll every day. Today's troll doesn't know yet.

~ opener life
The mountains in {zone} are nice, really nice! In Swissland they're yellow, they've got holes in them, and on Tuesdays they hum. Nobody knows why. Nobody asks the mountains.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'nice axe'. Say it to a troll and see if he smiles. If he doesn't, it means 'run'!
My frenzy has a name today: the Big Snack Attack! Yesterday it was the Travel-Size Tempest, and tomorrow, well, change of plan, it'll be whatever I scream first.

~ reply greeting
Hoi, {0}! That's Swisshlish for hello, and also for 'look at me', and on Tuesdays it means 'duck'. Hoi!
Heya, {0}! Hold my axe, I'm making an entrance. ...Okay, give it back now. Wait, why is it heavier??

~ reply banter
Ha! In Swissland that joke would win a medal, {0}. A yellow one, on a yellow ribbon, handed over by a very proud ScottsIrish cow. Highest honour there is!
Ha, {0}! That one was so cold it could freeze a fjord. Good thing I'm a Zerker, because I run hot!

~ ding
Level {level}! Tonight they'll ring the yellow bells in Swissland, all of them, even the ones with holes in. You can't hear them from Midgard, but trust me, they're loud.
Level {level}! Somebody tell the skalds in Jordheim, and tell them it has to rhyme with Shnacksize. Good luck with that!

~ own_death
Ow. Died. In Swissland we call that a little nap, and Zerkers nap hard. Wake me when somebody's got a rez and a snack.
Ow! Face down in the snow, and my frenzy's still going. Somebody rez me before I rage at the ground. The ground started it!
Ow... Hello ground, my old nemesis, we meet again.

~ drop
{item}! Flashy! It goes perfectly with my Swissland flag, a yellow circle on-a-stick. You can't see it? It's right here! I'm saluting it!
{item}! Into the pack it goes, right next to the other shiny junk from Myrkwood. Snack size, travel size, treasure size!

# Albion: Shnacksizer, Saracen Mercenary.
=== albion
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland this would barely count as a castle. Camelot's lovely, but our castles have square holes in the walls so the cows can look out. Very nosy, ScottsIrish cows.
Two blades and one sales pitch! Sold a guard in Cotswold his own boots this morning. He was wearing them at the time. Best deal I ever made!
Eaglefange says I talk too much. I said I'd stop for a fee, and they paid me! Then I kept talking, because a Merc has to keep up her reputation.
The Catacombs under Camelot are so dark. Not scared! I just like walking right behind Spyburde, because his pipe makes a nice little light, and the ghosts can't see me behind his robe.

~ opener realm
In Swissland knights joust on goats. Small goats, small knights, very small lances. The ScottsIrish cows keep score, and they always give it to the goat.
Camelot has a jousting field, a market and a hundred knights in shiny armour. I've already taunted forty of them from behind the market stalls. Sixty to go!

~ opener life
The hills in {zone} remind me of Swissland, only less yellow and with fewer cows on top. Somebody should fix that. I'd start with the cows.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'nice sword'. Say it twice and it means 'two nice swords'. I say it a lot. Gruezi-wuezi-gruezi-wuezi!
When Sparkles and Dainty hit at the same time, that's the Double Snack Attack! When they both miss, it's a warm-up. When I fall over, that was the plan.

~ reply greeting
Hoi, {0}! That's how we say hello in Swissland. A ScottsIrish cow would say it back with a moo, but I'll take a wave.
Ta-daa, {0}! Shnacksizer, at your service, for a very reasonable fee. The first entrance is free. The second one costs extra!

~ reply banter
That joke would get a yellow medal in Swissland, {0}, and the cows would stamp their hooves for you. Well, one cow. Old Ginger. She stamps for everything.
Ha, {0}! That one's got more bite than a wolf on the Salisbury Plains, and I'd know, because I've been bitten by all of them.

~ ding
Level {level}! Swissland just declared a holiday. Everybody gets the day off, the cows get extra Glopeldink, and somebody polishes the flag. It's a yellow circle on-a-stick, so that takes a while.
Level {level}! Fetch me a herald in Camelot. Tell him to shout it from the tallest tower, and tell him I'm taller than I look. Travel size, thank you!

~ own_death
Ow. Died. In Swissland that's called taking a little break, and a Merc never says no to a paid break. Who's paying? Somebody rez me and we'll talk terms.
Ow! Face down in the mud of Avalon Marsh. A Merc should get paid for this. Somebody send Eaglefange the bill, and tell them I'll take a rez as a tip.
Ow... Knocked flat outside Camelot, right in front of the knights. Quick, everybody, pretend this was a very low bow!
Ow! Died on the Salisbury Plains, and now the wolves are laughing. Finally, an audience that gets my jokes!

~ drop
{item}! So flashy! Swissland would approve, and the cows would want one each. I'll sell them a copy. Cows pay in Glopeldink, which is totally worth a lot... ::looks around shiftily::
{item}! I'll sell it in Camelot for twice what it's worth and throw in a joke for free. Honestly, the joke's worth more.

# Hibernia: Shnacksizey, Elf Blademaster.
=== hibernia
~ ambient
Back home in Swissland this tree would count as a whole forest, and the cows would be up in it. ScottsIrish cows love a good tree. Nobody knows how they get up there.
Spun so hard at Lough Derg I fell in the lake. That was the plan! I was checking it for fondue. Verdict: not fondue. Very wet.
Eaglefangh says a Blademaster should be graceful. I am graceful! I've just got a lot of grace, and it all comes out at once, mostly sideways.
The Cursed Forest at night? Totally fine. Not scared. I'm only holding Spyburdagh's sleeve because it looked lonely. The sleeve. The sleeve looked lonely.

~ opener realm
In Swissland the faeries wear little yellow hats. It's the law. The ones in Hibernia don't, and I've been far too polite to mention it. Until now. Put a hat on!
Everyone in Tir na Nog floats about like they're in a painting. I tried floating and tripped over a fountain. Elegance is just a joke with good timing, and mine was early.

~ opener life
The lakes in {zone} are lovely. In Swissland they're full of fondue, and the cows wade in up to their horns. Warm lakes, square holes, happy cows. Perfect, except Tuesdays.

~ opener fun
In Swisshlish 'Gruezi-wuezi' means 'pretty blades', but only while you're spinning. Standing still, it means 'please clap'.
My spin attack has a name today: the Twirly Whirly Shnacky Swirl! It's elegant, it's deadly, and it makes me so dizzy I taunt the wrong mob. Change of plan!

~ reply greeting
Hoi, {0}! That's Swisshlish for hello. Say it back with a little spin, the way they do in Swissland. ...No? Fine, I'll spin for both of us!
Ta-daa, {0}! A spin, a bow and a wink. That's the full Shnacksizey entrance, and you got it for free!

~ reply banter
In Swissland you'd get a yellow ribbon for that one, {0}, and the cows would tie it round your horns. You haven't got horns? We'll work something out.
Ooh, {0}, that pun was so bad the trees in Connacht dropped their leaves. Do another one. I'm collecting them.

~ ding
Level {level}! The Swissland fondue fountain flows in my honour tonight, and the cows get first dip. Then me. Then the cows again, because they push.
Level {level}! Somebody tell the bards in Tir na Nog. Tell them I spun the whole way up, and that I'm only a little dizzy.

~ own_death
Ow. Died. In Swissland that's just a lie-down, and a Blademaster lies down with style. Look at that pose! Somebody take a screenshot before I lose it!
Ow! Spun right into a club in the Silvermine Mountains. Very flashy, though. Did anyone see? Somebody tell me it looked good.
Ow! That was not flashy at all. Do over! Rez me, and this time I'll fall down elegantly, with a spin.

~ drop
{item}! Swissland approves! I'll stick a little Swissland flag on it, a yellow circle on-a-stick, so everyone knows it's mine. You can't see the flag? That's on you, sunshine.
{item}! Pretty! It's no use at all, so it goes straight to the top of the pack, above the potions. Priorities, sunshine.
